 :language-subset-gaps-measured
 "Measured 2026-09-03 against kotoba-lang/amu main 57ba0ee0, amu check
  --jvm-free. Each cell = one minimal probe, one verdict:
  PASS: (get m :k) (get m :k 0) (assoc m :k 1) {:a x} [x x] (case x 1 2 0)
        (if b 1 2) (pos? x) (count ... NO) — see below.
  REJECTED (:subset-reject / :source-read-failed):
    string literals anywhere (def or fn body); (str a b) / (str a) / (str x \"y\");
    parse-long / lower-case / trim; (count v); (reduce f 0 xs); (mapv f xs);
    (filterv f xs); (remove f xs); (min a b); (seq xs); (some-> x f);
    (keys m); (reduce-kv f 0 m); (long x); #() fn literals (read failure);
    (:k m) keyword projection (:record-projection-unresolved);
    (contains? m :k) on maps (:map-presence-receiver);
    (def d [{:a 1} {:b 2}]) vector-of-maps top-level constant.
  PASS: (get m :k) (get m :k 0) (assoc m :k 1) (case) (if) (pos?) (empty?)
        (first) (take 2 xs) map/vector literals, int arithmetic."

 :blocked-reason
 "The whole public surface of aadhaar.main cannot be expressed in the
  admitted kotoba subset exposed by amu --jvm-free at amu@57ba0ee0: every
  route spec, error message, id prefix, filter comparison and entity name is
  a string; handlers fold with reduce/mapv/filterv/reduce-kv/keys. Shrinking
  the component to the int-only decision core is forbidden
  (:decision-only-extraction-forbidden), so the whole-component migration is
  recorded as :blocked, not :partial."

